  "decision_summary": "L1/L2 gold-context and corroborating records uniformly support F≥20% for carboxylic-acid, uracil-dione, and fluorinated heteroaromatic analogs; L3 oral exposure records add human Cmax/AUC evidence for similar carboxylic-acid-containing molecules and contain no affirmative sub-20% signal. Physicochemical liabilities create uncertainty but do not constitute evidence for F<20%, so prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

